# Input fields

Every text-style input in the app (text, number, email, url, password, search)
must use the shared component:

```
src/components/HLInput.jsx
```

This is the React mirror of the HighRise `HLInput`. Do not hand-roll `<input>`
markup with bespoke sizing, and do not fork these styles into a page.

## Fixed design — never change

- **Size**: `sm` → 36px tall (`size="sm"`, i.e. `h-9` for any hand-rolled `<select>`
  that must visually match).
- **Corners**: 8px (`rounded-lg`).
- **Border**: `border-gray-300`; focus → `focus:border-primary-600`.
- **Text**: `text-[14px] text-gray-900`, `placeholder:text-gray-400`.
- **Padding**: `px-3` (or `pl-9 pr-3` when there is a leading icon via `prefixIcon`).
- **Disabled**: `disabled:bg-gray-50 disabled:text-gray-400`.

Do not use `h-8`/`h-10`, `rounded-md`, `border-gray-200` on form inputs/selects,
or `focus:border-primary-400`. If a design shows a different height or radius,
still use this sizing. (Toolbar filter/search chips are a deliberate exception —
see the `highrise-table` / `filter-styles` rules, which keep those at 32px.)

## Usage

```jsx
import HLInput from '../HLInput.jsx' // adjust relative depth

// Plain input
<HLInput size="sm" value={v} onChange={e => setV(e.target.value)} placeholder="Input text" />

// With a leading icon
<HLInput size="sm" prefixIcon={Globe} value={site} onChange={e => setSite(e.target.value)} placeholder="e.g. hubspot.com" />

// Non-input elements that must match (e.g. a <select>) — hand-roll the same spec
<select className="w-full h-9 px-3 pr-8 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white text-[14px] text-gray-900 outline-none appearance-none focus:border-primary-600 transition-colors cursor-pointer">…</select>
```

## Label pattern — every labeled field, everywhere

The label directly above a form input or dropdown is always:

```
text-[14px] font-medium mb-1
```

(`mb-1` = 4px gap between the label and the field below it.) Label color may be
`text-gray-500` or `text-gray-700` depending on the surrounding form, but size
(14px), weight (medium), and the 4px gap are fixed. Never use `text-[12px]` or
`text-[13px]` for a field label, and never use `mb-2`/`mb-1.5`/`mb-3` between a
label and its own input — that 4px gap is reserved for label→field only, not
for a label→helper-paragraph→input chain (a helper/description line between
label and field may keep its own spacing).

- `HLInput` forwards all native props (`value`, `onChange`, `placeholder`,
  `type`, `disabled`, `autoFocus`, `maxLength`, `prefixIcon`, `suffix`, …).
- `<textarea>` and `<select>` are not `HLInput`, but must match its
  radius/border/focus/height (36px) — hand-roll the same classes shown above.

## Do not

- Do not build an input with raw `<input className="…custom…">` when `HLInput` fits.
- Do not change the height, radius, border color, or focus color per usage.
- Do not leave a `<select>` at 32px (`h-8`) or 40px (`h-10`) next to `HLInput`
  fields at 36px — every labeled field in the same form must be the same height.
- Do not leave a field label at 12px/13px or with more than a 4px gap to its input.
